    "result_text": "A held claim now counts in claimed again. Only the due figures leave it out while it's held. `bin/e2e` passes all 4 tests in the spec; before the change, the main one failed because Ben's claimed showed `0.00` instead of `30.00` while his claim was held.\n\n**Server** (`src/main/java/net/officefloor/hq/app/rollup/Rollup.java`):\n- Claimed, the claimed-total and the ROLLUP and TOTALS audit lines now include a claim held by itself or by its person's hold. A claim still drops out of claimed when it's deferred, when its status doesn't count, or when its person has retired.\n- A held claim is still left out of the due-total and overdue-total. Settled-total, open-total, the period figures and the carried figures also still leave it out, as before.\n- I removed the old `countsLive` check, which nothing used any more.\n\n**Front end** (`src/main/frontend/src/app/core/claims.ts`): the person's claimed and the claimed-total now follow the same rule as the server. The due totals still use the existing list that leaves held claims out.\n\nI also updated the comments on `Claim.held` and `ClaimService.toggleHold` to match. No database change was needed.\n\nOne choice I made: retirement still takes a claim out of claimed. The request only mentioned holds, but retirement used the same check in the code, so I split them apart.",
